  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Installation of a double sided communications hub.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed communication hub, by reason of its excessive scale, siting and design, within a constrained section of the public footway, would result in an unnecessary and harmful addition to the streetscape. The cumulative impact of these features would detract from the established character of the street and diminish the quality of the public realm. The proposal is therefore contrary to London Plan Policy D8 (Public Realm), Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character) and CC5 (Advertisement Panels, Hoardings and Structures), and the aims of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed communication hub, by reason of its excessive scale, siting and design within an already constrained section of the public footway and in close proximity to busy junction, would result in unacceptable harm to pedestrian and highway safety. The development would therefore be contrary to Local Plan Policy EC2 (Developing a Sustainable Local Transport Network) and Policy CC5 (Advertisement Panels, Hoardings and Structures)."
  ],
